==============================================================================================================
C. The anchors: how much of each rail the clock can remove, and how leakage falls with voltage
==============================================================================================================
(i) aifoundry2 idle: 35.0 W at 800 MHz / 0.618 V (die [64, 65] C) against 28.1 W at 600 MHz / 0.517 V (die [63, 68] C) [measured]; against the idle law at 64.5 C (27.66 W) the step is 7.34 W, raw 6.90 W: anchor 7.12 +- 0.72 W at the board
    the same governor points in E51 (aifoundry2, 28 Sep), median on die: minion 618 / 519 mV, SRAM 830 / 704 mV at 800 / 600 MHz (5282 and 40147 samples) [measured]: the SRAM rail steps too, and its step is part of the anchor
(ii) at a 62 C die: card 0 (1.4.1, 300 MHz, minion 0.399 V, SRAM 0.66 V) minion 4.091 W, SRAM 0.879, NoC 2.750 W; aifoundry2 (600 MHz, 0.519 V) minion 8.302 W, SRAM 1.336, NoC 2.698 W [measured]
     the NoC rails, same voltage and clock on both, agree to 1.019: the two chips leak alike; minion ratio corrected for it: 0.483 +- 10 % (the anchor)
     check at 67 C, aifoundry3 over aifoundry2: NoC rail x1.048, minion rail x1.054 at 522 against 518 mV [measured]
     check at 67 C, aifoundry1-c1 over aifoundry2: NoC rail x1.561, minion rail x1.400 at 499 against 518 mV [measured]
     card 0's own temperature slopes at 60-64 C: minion 0.100, SRAM 0.0166, NoC 0.054 W/C; aifoundry2 at 62 C: minion 0.236, SRAM 0.0442 W/C [measured]
shared minion clock tree at 600 MHz and 518 mV: the values at which every card's refit stays within 1.5x its best rms: 0.84-2.24 W (65 grid values of 0.01 W) [fitted]
shared noc clock tree (NoC at 400 MHz) and 484 mV: the values at which every card's refit stays within 1.5x its best rms: 0.02-0.42 W (29 grid values of 0.01 W) [fitted]

anchors: 12 % of prior draws pass (i), 25 % pass (ii), 94 % keep every refitted rail within 1.5x its best rms, 2 % pass all; the first 2000 are kept
kappa_m (minion leakage, per volt) [fitted]: 2 / 2.49 / 2.93  (prior 0.5-8; N7 DIBL-only 1.4 [outside, O11])
minion leakage at 398 mV over 518 mV, G = (V/V0) e^(kappa (V-V0)) [fitted]: 0.543 / 0.572 / 0.607;  DIBL-only [outside]: 0.65
minion leakage at 618 mV over 518 mV [fitted]: 1.46 / 1.54 / 1.61
minion clock tree at 600 MHz / 518 mV [fitted]: 0.889 / 1.69 / 2.22 W (correlation with kappa -0.67); NoC clock tree at 400 MHz: 0.0284 / 0.206 / 0.407 W
   aifoundry2     leakage T_L, minion 31 / 33 / 35 C, SRAM 25 / 28 / 31 C, NoC 32 / 34 / 35 C; SRAM clock tree 0.0395 / 0.242 / 0.445 W [fitted]
   aifoundry3     leakage T_L, minion 30 / 32 / 35 C, SRAM 39 / 41 / 44 C, NoC 31 / 33 / 35 C; SRAM clock tree 0.0456 / 0.234 / 0.36 W [fitted]
   aifoundry1-c1  leakage T_L, minion 31 / 32 / 34 C, SRAM 30 / 35 / 39 C, NoC 32 / 33 / 34 C; SRAM clock tree 0.858 / 1.05 / 1.3 W [fitted]
check (not an anchor): at 67 C, aifoundry3's minion rail over aifoundry2's, corrected to 518 mV with the fitted kappa: x1.035, against its NoC rail's x1.048: the NoC rail tracks a chip's leakage [measured/model]
check (not an anchor): at 67 C, aifoundry1-c1's minion rail over aifoundry2's, corrected to 518 mV with the fitted kappa: x1.523, against its NoC rail's x1.561: the NoC rail tracks a chip's leakage [measured/model]
kappa_s (SRAM leakage, per volt) [fitted, through anchor (i)]: 1.5 / 2.6 / 4.5 (prior 1.4-10); the SRAM rail's part of the 800 MHz step 0.728 / 1.02 / 1.57 W (of 7.12 +- 0.72)
SRAM leakage at 660 mV over 704 mV [fitted]: 0.769 / 0.836 / 0.878
anchor tension: (i) alone passes 12.3 % of the prior, (ii) alone 25.1 %, both 2.5 %; card 0's 1.4.1 low-power state may not be a pure change of voltage and clock [inference]
check (not an anchor): card 0's SRAM rail over aifoundry2's at 62 C, model 0.681 / 0.756 / 0.843, measured 0.66; the SRAM rails do not follow the NoC rails between cards (aifoundry3's is 1.84x aifoundry2's at 62 C), so the model keeps the wider range [measured/model]
check (not an anchor): card 0's minion temperature slope at 62 C, model (its leakage over aifoundry2's T_L) 0.108 / 0.109 / 0.112 W/C, measured 0.100; a larger T_L at low voltage would make the model's slopes at the floor a little high, i.e. pessimistic [model/measured]

==============================================================================================================
D. The decomposition of idle and loaded power, per card, at its own operating point
==============================================================================================================
Board power at the card's own point = (a) the part no minion clock or voltage touches (off the metered rails: SP, PCIe, memory shires and DRAM, IO, Maxion, board and regulator losses; plus the NoC rail at its own clock) + (b) minion and SRAM leakage (+ its regulator loss) + (c) the minion and SRAM clock tree at idle (+ loss).
(a) is the measured law less (b) and (c); (b) and (c) come from the per-rail fits (section B) [fitted/model]; the regulator loss of (b) and (c) is counted with them.
  aifoundry2 (600 MHz, 518/704 mV) die   25 C: board  17.4 W = (a) 11.9 / 12.2 / 12.7 + (b) 2.53 / 2.9 / 3.41 + (c) 1.28 / 2.24 / 2.94 W; (c) is 7.4 / 12.9 / 16.9 %  [model]
  aifoundry2 (600 MHz, 518/704 mV) die   40 C: board  20.0 W = (a) 12.9 / 13.2 / 13.5 + (b) 4.14 / 4.64 / 5.29 + (c) 1.28 / 2.24 / 2.94 W; (c) is 6.4 / 11.2 / 14.7 %  [model]
  aifoundry2 (600 MHz, 518/704 mV) die   60 C: board  25.8 W = (a) 14.7 / 15 / 15.2 + (b) 7.99 / 8.66 / 9.51 + (c) 1.28 / 2.24 / 2.94 W; (c) is 5.0 / 8.6 / 11.4 %  [model]
  aifoundry2 (600 MHz, 518/704 mV) die   73 C: board  31.8 W = (a) 16.2 / 16.6 / 16.8 + (b) 12.2 / 13 / 14 + (c) 1.28 / 2.23 / 2.94 W; (c) is 4.0 / 7.0 / 9.2 %  [model]
  aifoundry3 (600 MHz, 522/698 mV) die   25 C: board  18.9 W = (a) 12.8 / 13.1 / 13.4 + (b) 3.25 / 3.68 / 4.27 + (c) 1.28 / 2.2 / 2.87 W; (c) is 6.7 / 11.6 / 15.2 %  [model]
