loaded, aifoundry2 at 80 C, fp32 randn on 1,024 minions: 63.9 W at the board [measured, dvfs.json busy_randn_80c] = (a) 17.6 + (b) 16.2 + (c) 2.2 + switching 27.6 W [measured: busy - idle 36.3] (medians; (a)-(c) model): the switching is 43 %, the clock tree 3 %; at 100 MHz and the floor voltages the switching would be 2.7 W [model]
check against Esperanto's measured idle (outside O3, RISC-V Summit 2022: card 20.0 W, minion 5.8, NoC 1.6, SRAM 1.7 W; clock and temperature not given): aifoundry2's model reaches a 5.8 W minion rail at a 46 C die, where its NoC rail is 1.75 W, its SRAM rail 0.91 W (Esperanto: 1.7) and the card 21.5 W [model/outside]; 46 C lies below every measured bin of aifoundry2 (62-84 C), so these are its fitted laws extrapolated
loaded: fp32 randn TensorFMA adds 22.7 / 25.5 / 28.3 W at the board on 32 shires at 600 MHz (measured +27.1 on aifoundry2, 10-data-dependent-power.md) [measured/assumed range]; x f V^2: at 100 MHz and 398 mV 2.24 / 2.52 / 2.8 W, at 10 MHz 0.224 / 0.252 / 0.28 W [model]

