==============================================================================================================
read docs/reports/data/2026-09-30-without-heatsink/imaging_calc.json (seed 20260930, 240 draws)
the camera's reading per kelvin (medians, imaging_calc.json): (b) lid top, taped, fan 0.845; (b) lid top, taped, still air 0.845; (a) delidded die, black-coated, IR-window cooler 0.634
check: taped lid, fan, checkerboard at 100 MHz / 398 mV: 29 s by scaling the least power; the imaging model's own median at 100 MHz / 398 mV: 29 s
A look of 10 s or less needs no steady state: with the heatsink on, 512 minions of random data (13.6 W, about 16 shires) took 84 s from 80 to 90 C (12-heat-management.md) [measured]; bare, section F2 gives the seconds from the end of the host boot to 85 C with the pattern running (median) [model].
Per settable point (aifoundry2's voltages): per-shire switching power; for each view, whether a sustained 16-shire pattern settles below 85 C (share of draws), and per pattern the camera's apparent contrast in a 1 s-per-state difference image (mK, emissivity applied, product of medians) and the lock-in time to SNR 3 (median; "<=" = an upper bound; 10 = 10 s or less).  Sensors: contrast in real mK at the transistor plane.  [model]
